{"title":"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Recognition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Recognition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math_(FAST)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Continuum Math (FAST)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A real-valued function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> has the property that for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1d6265e67657b5886ce257671d45ff9c0282eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bd7b5dc604674f392920ae5bd0a29c5ebbf73d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a + b)  + f(a - b) = 2f(a) f(b).\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" /> Which one of the following cannot be the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be194f19302b30f020505bcc879acd7a996679e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa3fcc22d44b8d9d46d54d54447ababb0af9154c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } -1 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"400\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cdad33e067510298b8f671157d89556ea3aadb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2a) + f(0) = 2f(a)^2\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc6f6fb88fa3d4ba4841f4b055fa3ddb7b99f27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a= 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03d4c990a866c07ed0ed78c64bfa5e4a9209ca14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2f(0) = 2f(0)^2 \\implies f(0) \\in \\{0, 1\\}.\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"20\" />\nThis gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c51450ee6d0ae690f78ca2ff96eb73d9dee0be4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2a) = 2f(a)^2 - f(0) \\geq 0-1\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/584468cd4c65823de9a250fe030f827bce3f7a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e652bf09419c2d6821e3e02509d540114d0fe8c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) \\geq -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, so answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f732efd292433efb20fa7e55d3eda4b7519f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) -2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"30\" /> is impossible. \n</p><p>~AtharvNaphade\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe4f650cef35716c9656aeb91ebf8723a2869638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leftarrow 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c8580def7187108fffa608854eb540d3163babe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leftarrow 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />.\nThus, the equation given in the problem becomes \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/0951f0a4e03b61917281b9f7ddabeec7a97da55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ f(0) + f(0) = 2 f(0) \\times f(0) . ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c59bd9d20bcc9cd7fea79dd1f88c8d6332ce55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> or 1.\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c59bd9d20bcc9cd7fea79dd1f88c8d6332ce55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c8580def7187108fffa608854eb540d3163babe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leftarrow 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />.\nThus, the equation given in the problem becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/baea5bc16771d712e22905d98b94e572fee8d0a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ 2 f(a) = 0 . ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c6d50cc225dfa25d1a271764d69412ff0d42987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf24e88058a6fdef1dddad3aa7562a7cf7109b32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f648e7356d8fce99d0cad3e838cbd76b833369.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leftarrow a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />.\nThus, the equation given in the problem becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b01a2b48d8c9d52b836d4a54b7a51b48296981e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ f(2a) + 1 = 2 \\left( f(a) \\right)^2. ]\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Thus, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca252307c2e6cbd8dca28e4e14866d44c26f3dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(2a) &amp; = -1 + 2 \\left( f(a) \\right)^2 \\\\ &amp; \\geq -1 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"180\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, an infeasible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5b19bf7575fdc3655bb5767980f09dbb747a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f34f6042667812f3b3fc7cd6e3a742b3087ecf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) -2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"68\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com) kk choudhary\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The relationship looks suspiciously like a product-to-sum identity. In fact,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83339b271f57a6512e06f0694e03744825aadf0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) = \\frac{1}{2}(\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)+\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta))\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"37\" />\nwhich is basically the relation. So we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2644cc9ce7c9379a1398bed5ce9626ba5491d9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> is a valid solution to the function. However, if we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d019c8367ae85af7c39460e224253268a8bd1db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=ay,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is arbitrary, the above relation should still hold for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a07029a1e41be9112201282f9facd9925bfa554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\cos(ay) = \\cos(a(1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" /> so any value in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39f506ebeeeb72f62147990614a67f4e30b7c751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-1,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> can be reached, so choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74ae5f3d2d5c9a0767f5fae081c4f77ee78f2d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are incorrect.\n</p><p>In addition, using the similar formula for hyperbolic cosine, we know\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc701a8473efb30a842cf0cb52450859bd1972e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cosh(\\alpha)\\cosh(\\beta) = \\frac{1}{2}(\\cosh(\\alpha-\\beta)+\\cosh(\\alpha+\\beta))\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"37\" />\nThe range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/8295d5d8107af252ea178da261b20b782de9ed39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cosh(ay)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f9905999da1cecf33b5bd8d8c04f3fbfc533878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1,\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" /> so choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is incorrect.\n</p><p>Therefore, the remaining answer is choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f34f6042667812f3b3fc7cd6e3a742b3087ecf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) -2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"68\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~kxiang\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Recognition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Recognition)\">Solution 4 (Recognition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Recognition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 3 we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97fb2626c0f3f0b04b0c2fbf1359b2d6bb29fe99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos (a - b) \\cos (a + b) = \\cos (a)\\cos(b).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"288\" height=\"20\" /> \nDoing testing gives us that any function in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41c38d2b4cebcd3b64367865a2655ecb2a1f7f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(bx)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> works. We now see that only 2 and -2 are the candidates to be impossible. \nSolving the functional equation the regular way, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/3093de224ed6a7c430a29dc970a119c4f7fdc429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 1, f(-x) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />. We eventually get a squared term (from even more testing), and see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c099cc1037ebf74d422f1358037f67ffbb2beba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{-2 (E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"32\" /> is the answer because negative square roots are impossible.\n</p><p>~Aarav22\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hBf_SVKK9tE\">https://youtu.be/hBf_SVKK9tE</a> \n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UML6WmL0mNk\">https://youtu.be/UML6WmL0mNk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GK0ZpjxbwLw\">https://youtu.be/GK0ZpjxbwLw</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math_.28FAST.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math_(FAST)\">Video Solution by Continuum Math (FAST)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Continuum Math (FAST)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/R-zrBkVx48Q\">https://youtu.be/R-zrBkVx48Q</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B\">2023 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems\" tit